-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/8e2ad77c-85e7-4843-ac9b-47707b3bf88d
-- title:
--   Half holding makes a stationary Markov quadratic form nonnegative
-- statement:
--   Let $\Omega$ be finite, let $\pi$ be a probability distribution on $\Omega$, and let $P$ be a Markov transition matrix with $\pi P=\pi$. Assume $P(x,x)\ge1/2$ for every state. For every real function $f:\Omega\to\mathbb R$,
--
--   $$\langle f,Pf\rangle_\pi
--   =\sum_{x,y}\pi(x)P(x,y)f(x)f(y)\ge0.$$
--
--   Here $\langle f,g\rangle_\pi=\sum_x\pi(x)f(x)g(x)$. Reversibility and full support of $\pi$ are not hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/IdealChainNonnegDefinite.lean#L13-L56

